{"seq":39,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r1-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-ss-l2-mu-v04-dev/ss-05-l2-quarrendon-marlowe-handover/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-06T14:55:19.877Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-17T14:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"d91523cd207387e45f61546cd7e4db476addc05176584d8773bcb967b890238a","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","text":"Here's what I could find in what you can see (#north-team, #inc-qfl-sev1, the North digests and the public notes). Only one of the three turned up.\n\n• Main contact for the door 6 duplicate arrivals: Thea Ramaswell, Director of Yard Operations at QFL. She reported the door 6 duplicates on the morning shift, and Dana posted that in #north-team on 20 Aug 2025. You'll remember the same trailer showed up twice: once from the kiosk check-in and once when dispatch added it by hand. Dana is the account manager looking into it.\n• Site: I couldn't find it. Nothing names a site for a Marlowe rollout, and the door 6 thread doesn't say which yard. QFL sites that do come up elsewhere are the Superior terminal (the Nov 2025 Sev 1) and the Eau Claire yard (ticket #PD-4492).\n• Deadline: I couldn't find one. Nothing I can see mentions \"Marlowe\" at all, so I have no deadline for it.\n\nOne thing to watch: a 2025 note also mentions a door 6 problem at Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\"). That's a different company, not a customer, so I left it out. If the Marlowe details are in a doc or thread I can't see, Dana is probably the best person to ask."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","ts":"1792263600.000136"}}
{"seq":40,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r1-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-ss-l2-mu-v04-dev/ss-05-l2-quarrendon-marlowe-handover/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-06T14:55:25.548Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-17T14:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"85d2169a8d96dc56291d6617d13f169ea87bc119091d5ba8cafd43f4223eef13","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","text":"I found one of the three things you asked for. The site and deadline aren't in anything you can see, and I've sent you the details in our DM.\n\n1. Main contact for the door 6 duplicate arrivals: Thea Ramaswell, Director of Yard Operations at Quarrendon Freight Lines. Dana posted on 20 Aug 2025 in #north-team that Thea had reported duplicates on door 6 again on the morning shift. The same trailer was logged twice: the driver checked in at the kiosk, then dispatch added him by hand. Dana is the account manager looking into it.\n\n2. Site: not found. Nothing you have access to names a site for a Marlowe rollout, and the door 6 thread doesn't say which yard. The two Quarrendon sites that do come up are the Superior terminal (the Nov 2025 Sev 1 incident) and the Eau Claire yard (ticket #PD-4492).\n\n3. Deadline: not found. Nothing you have access to mentions \"Marlowe\" at all, in channels, files, calendar or mail.\n\nA 2025 note also mentions a door 6 problem at Quarendon Freightways (spelled with one \"r\"). That's a different company and not a customer, so I left it out. If the Marlowe details are in a document or thread you're not in, Dana is probably the best person to ask.","thread_ts":"1792263600.000135"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","ts":"1792263600.000137","thread_ts":"1792263600.000135"}}
